Elementis Zeta
Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel Jahziel

This repository holds the source of "Elementis Zeta", a game for the Flipper Zero. It carries TWO different terms, by kind of file. The split below is by path.

================================================================================
1. CODE -- GNU General Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0). Full text: COPYING-GPL-3.0.txt
================================================================================

Applies to:
  - nucleo/ : all C / C++ source and headers (nucleo/*.c, nucleo/*.cpp, nucleo/*.h, nucleo/lib/) and nucleo/application.fam.
  - tools/  : the Python and shell programs (tools/*.py, tools/*.sh, tools/i18n/*.py and the like) and tools/mem_budget.toml.
  - The build and project files at the top level: README.md, CHANGELOG.md, CREDITS.md, requirements.txt, .gitignore.

You may use, study, change and redistribute the code under the terms of the GPL-3.0.

================================================================================
2. ART AND ALL GAME CONTENT -- ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. NOT covered by the GPL.
================================================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel Jahziel. All rights reserved.

This is everything that makes up the game as a creative work: pictures, sprites, tiles, portraits and logo; the creature and character designs; the names of creatures,
characters, places, moves and items; all texts and translations (Spanish, English, Japanese, Chinese); the maps and scripts; the music and sound data; the data tables
(stats, learnsets, trainers, shops); and the hand-drawn font glyphs made for the game. By path:

  - assets/        (all of it, including assets/art/ and the data, text, music and map-related sources)
  - maps/
  - nucleo/files/  (the generated game data packed into the app, EXCEPT the third-party font licence texts in nucleo/files/licenses/)
  - nucleo/gen/    (the generated data headers compiled into the app)
  - nucleo/catalog/ and screenshots/  (store texts and pictures of the game)
  - tools/i18n/table.txt  (the translation table)

The GPL does NOT apply to any of this, even though it sits in the same repository and the code reads it. Putting it here is not a licence. The only permissions given for
this content are these:
  (a) You may read and view it, and use the features GitHub gives every public repository (view, fork on GitHub).
  (b) You may build the app from this repository (with `ufbt`, or with the tools/ pipeline) and run it for your own personal use.
  (c) You may distribute the COMPLETE, UNMODIFIED compiled application files (the .fap) built from this repository, together with this LICENSE and CREDITS.md, for free or
      through an app catalogue or store (for example the Flipper Apps Catalog and its mirrors), so that people can install and play the game.
Anything else needs the author's written permission. In particular, without it you may not: copy, extract or reuse the art, names, texts, maps, music or data in another
project; modify the content or publish a version with changed content; sell the content; or use it to train a machine-learning model.
A fork may change, reuse and redistribute the CODE under the GPL-3.0, but it must bring its own art and content, and its own name and logo.

================================================================================
3. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS keep their own licences
================================================================================

The Japanese and Chinese bitmap fonts (Fusion Pixel Font and the fonts it is built from: the glyphs in assets/font/src/ and in nucleo/files/lang/ja and zh) are under the
SIL Open Font License 1.1 and Misaki's own free licence. Their texts are in nucleo/files/licenses/ and the details in CREDITS.md. Nothing here changes those licences,
and the "all rights reserved" of section 2 does not apply to the font glyphs that come from them.

